{
  "_readme": [
    "HAND-COMPUTED team standings for G6. Not generated from lib/scoring/ \u2014 a fixture derived",
    "from the code under test proves nothing.",
    "",
    "This fixture exists to pin ONE formula (docs/SCORING.md \u00a71):",
    "",
    "  teamScore = (sum of all player points, group problems included) / teamSize",
    "              + sideActivityPoints",
    "",
    "PANTHERS is the organizer's real worked example, taken from an actual scoring sheet:",
    "players at 400, 250, 400, 400, one 125-point group problem, side activities 20 + 80 + 50.",
    "",
    "  individual sum  400 + 250 + 400 + 400 = 1450",
    "  group                                 =  125",
    "  team size                             =    4",
    "  side activities 20 + 80 + 50          =  150",
    "  teamScore = (1450 + 125) / 4 + 150 = 393.75 + 150 = 543.75",
    "",
    "CUBS is a team of TWO, and it is here because the divisor is the whole point. A formula",
    "that ignored team size would rank a small team as though it were a large one.",
    "",
    "  individual 300 + 100 = 400, group 100 partial, size 2, side 0",
    "  teamScore = (400 + 100) / 2 + 0 = 250",
    "",
    "Specific traps each row is here to catch:",
    "  pan-2   partial credit on a WA still scores 150. Not every scoring point comes from an AC.",
    "  pan-3   submits G1 as well as pan-1, both scoring 125. A group problem is solved ONCE by",
    "          the team, so the team gets 125 and not 250. Summing per-member group scores is the",
    "          obvious wrong implementation.",
    "  cub-1   partial credit on a GROUP problem: 100 of 125.",
    "  orphan  has NO team and scores 400. Must contribute to no team total anywhere. A",
    "          participant with a null teamId is the shape a mid-contest roster edit leaves behind."
  ],
